+# spec-v2-dublin-spawn-director — the district spawn-director (Dublin arc, stage 2 job 1)
+
+Job: `packet-plumber-v2-dublin-spawn-director`. User directive 2026-08-24:
+"game play and node spawn must match the decisions made for the map
+beautify". The 7-round lavish mock gate's rulings are CANON.
+
+## 0. Canon (read from the approved artifacts — never assumed)
+
+- **Density ruling:** `data/maps/dublin.json` → `rulings.density_default =
+  "1in6"` (user blessed ~1-in-6 as the calm default at board zoom; baked by
+  the #90 spike gate, memlog 2026-08-23: "user APPROVE + density 1in6").
+  The pool IS the stride-6 subsample of the asset's street-adjacent points
+  (snapped + deduped + grid-filtered at load: **603 pool tiles** — the
+  loader's own census, printed by the dublin-grown verb; a Python round()
+  census miscounted 602: the loader uses C-style math.round, which differs
+  on .5 boundaries).
+- **Zoom-band model (approved Round 7):** zoomed OUT = neighborhoods as
+  blobs + only the backbone (arterial spine); zoomed IN = dense houses +
+  last-mile web. The gallery's density gradient: city core densest,
+  periphery sparser (KYLE reads of `docs/captures/dublin-map-mock/`).
+- **Cluster shapes:** estates anchored in real neighborhoods — the 08-21
+  STRICT estate doctrine (ATTACH within radius_tiles of a cluster member /
+  SEED at ≥ new_area_seed_tiles from every live terminal; cap 5 members,
+  radius 5 tiles) is the approved cluster shape, already shipped.
+- **Building conformity:** street-aligned blocks. Spawn side = the pool is
+  street-adjacent by construction (bake-time STRtree frontage). Done in
+  stage 1; unchanged here.
+- **Stage-1 warning (map.odin header, load-bearing):** a district-SCOPED
+  ATTACH draw would starve ~63% of pool tiles at the 1-in-6 snap (the
+  Voronoi cells are smaller than the estate radius 5). The district policy
+  must therefore NOT scope the attach ring; it weights the CLUSTER PICK.
+- **Streets-constrain-pipes + last-mile draw: OUT (stage-2 jobs 2/3).**
+  Render/zoom-LOD bands: OUT (spawn side only).
+
+## 1. Design
+
+### 1.1 Load-time per-tile district assignment (map.odin)
+
+`Map_Board` gains a derived assignment (pure function of the loaded bytes —
+deterministic, re-created identically on replay):
+
+- `tile_district: [dynamic]u16` — for every `candidates[k]`, the index of
+  its nearest district anchor (Euclidean², tie-break = lower district
+  index — file order, deterministic; ODN-10: integer math on tile-scaled
+  anchor positions).
+- `district_tiles: [dynamic][dynamic]u32` — per-district index lists into
+  `candidates` (the SEED family's per-district draw domain). Districts with
+  zero tiles simply hold an empty list (the weighted pick skips them by
+  construction).
+- `district_assign(pos) -> u16` — the nearest-anchor lookup for an ARBITRARY
+  tile (used for per-terminal district counting + the ATTACH cluster-pick
+  weight). One linear scan over ≤ 52 anchors — trivial.
+
+The stage-1 note ("A future district-scoped policy re-adds the assignment +
+ranges as data") is exactly this: assignment in the board, ranges in
+balance.json.
+
+### 1.2 The SEED family becomes district-weighted (growth.odin)
+
+Board branch only. Draw sequence per SEED attempt (replaces the single
+uniform pool draw `growth_board_seed_draw`):
+
+1. Build the ELIGIBLE district list: districts with `tile_district` pool
+   tiles AND live-terminal count < the district cap (the cap contract —
+   §1.4). Weights = the district kind's `seed_weight_permille`
+   (balance.json `growth_districts`; 0 = the band is excluded).
+2. ONE weighted_pick over the eligible list (skipped when exactly one
+   eligible district — the draw-count rule mirrors the cluster-pick
+   precedent: `rng_range`/`weighted_pick` draws nothing for a 1-element
+   choice... weighted_pick is a SINGLE rng draw; when `eligible == 1` the
+   pick is skipped and the one district wins without drawing, matching the
+   existing `rng_range(0, eligible-1)` skip semantics). All weights ≤ 0 →
+   no eligible district → the attempt fails WITHOUT drawing (deterministic
+   rejection — the window budget covers it).
+3. ONE uniform tile draw within the picked district's tile list (skipped
+   when the district holds one tile — same rule).
+4. The E31 + fresh-area predicates gate below, UNCHANGED.
+
+Estate labeling: the seed's tile carries its district assignment — the
+estate anchors to its real neighborhood (the approved cluster-anchor
+semantic, now data-backed instead of the label-only nearest-anchor).
+
+### 1.3 The ATTACH family becomes district-weighted (growth.odin)
+
+Board branch only. The ring draw stays GLOBAL (the stage-1 starvation
+constraint — the streets rule is untouched: an estate forms on the streets
+the grid gives it). The district weighting lives in the CLUSTER PICK:
+
+- The eligible-cluster scan gains TWO predicates: (a) the district of the
+  cluster's FIRST MEMBER (its seed district — deterministic: nearest anchor
+  of the first-member slot's position) must be under its cap; (b) the
+  existing ring-room predicate stays.
+- The cluster pick becomes ONE weighted_pick over the eligible clusters with
+  weight = the cluster's seed district's kind weight (skipped when one
+  eligible cluster — same draw-count rule as today). Same draw COUNT as the
+  current uniform pick (one draw) — the interleaving shifts only through
+  the acceptance outcome + the weight values.
+
+So: core estates (city/town/quarter) extend eagerly; backbone estates
+(suburb/neighbourhood) cap at 5 members and yield to SEED — the band model
+compounds at both families.
+
+### 1.4 District caps (the density ruling as a hard bound)
+
+`growth_districts.district_cap_permille` — the district's live-terminal
+budget as a permille of its own 1-in-6 pool share:
+
+```
+cap(district d) = max(1, floor(pool_tiles(d) × district_cap_permille / 1000))
+```
+
+- Default **1000** = the blessed 1-in-6 fabric: a district never grows more
+  live terminals than its own pool tiles (the density ceiling). The knob is
+  the user's density iteration surface (e.g. ~667 ≈ the 1-in-9 fabric).
+- Live-terminal counting: per window, count live terminals whose nearest
+  anchor == the district (a derived scan — pure function of (topology,
+  board), zero rng; slot-order deterministic). The budget is the LIVE count
+  (the estate-view precedent) — the freeing clause is vacuous-by-design
+  (r1 W2): terminal demolish is E2-forbidden, so the count is monotone
+  within a run.
+- **The hard bound covers the DRAWN TILE too (r1 W1):** the attach branch
+  cap-checks the drawn candidate's OWN district (a cross-boundary attach
+  places the member in a neighboring district — the estate straddles
+  Voronoi cells by design, so the member's district is the one that must
+  have budget). Zero draws — a rejection predicate like E31 (the bounded
+  attempt budget covers it). Pinned by
+  test_growth_dublin_attach_tile_district_cap.
+- The cap gates BOTH families: a capped district is excluded from the SEED
+  weighted pick AND its clusters are ineligible for ATTACH. Full board
+  (every district at cap) → every attempt rejects deterministically →
+  growth stops. This is the density ceiling doing its job, not a stall.
+
+### 1.5 The zoom-band model = the kind tier (data)
+
+The approved zoom behavior maps to the district KIND tier (the data's own
+label class): City/Town/Quarter = the dense-core band (richer), Village/
+Suburb/Neighbourhood = the backbone band (sparser). Weights are named
+tunables — the user fun-tests and iterates (rule 3). Proposed defaults:
+
+| kind | seed_weight_permille | band |
+|---|---|---|
+| city | 4 | dense-core |
+| town | 3 | dense-core |
+| quarter | 3 | dense-core |
+| village | 2 | backbone (sparse) |
+| suburb | 1 | backbone (sparse) |
+| neighbourhood | 1 | backbone (sparse) |
+
+The per-TILE seed rate (weight ÷ pool tiles) then reads: city 0.8 vs suburb
+0.002 — the core is ~400× richer per tile than the suburban fabric, which
+is the "dense-core districts richer" ruling, while the absolute map still
+reads suburban-dominant (517 of 603 pool tiles — the loader census) — the gallery's read.
+
+### 1.6 Determinism story (rule 1 + scope 3)
+
+- The director state is a PURE FUNCTION of (board bytes, catalog, topology,
+  seed): the assignment is load-time-derived from the same bytes (replay
+  re-creates it identically — the fixture precedent), the caps/weights ride
+  the catalog_hash, the live counts derive from the topology. **Nothing new
+  is serialized; LOG_VERSION is NOT bumped** — the map_source byte already
+  pins the map input in the T1 hash (absent-when-procedural) and the spawned
+  terminals ride the topology section. Documented in the PR body.
+- **Old runs pin:** procedural runs never enter the board branch — zero
+  rng-draw change, byte-identical (the full 48-golden suite proves it).
+- **Dublin re-bless (cause-documented):** the board branch's SEED family
+  changes from 1 draw to ≤2 draws (district pick + tile pick) and the
+  ATTACH cluster pick changes from uniform to weighted (same draw count) —
+  the rng interleaving shifts on dublin runs BY DESIGN. `dublin_board.dem`
+  re-blesses with the cause stated; every `.log.bin`/`.t1` change verified
+  byte-exact vs HEAD.
+
+## 2. Data (balance.json — `growth_districts`)
+
+```json
+"growth_districts": {
+  "_comment": "the district spawn-director (Dublin arc stage-2 job 1): ...",
+  "district_cap_permille": 1000,
+  "seed_weight_city": 4,
+  "seed_weight_town": 3,
+  "seed_weight_village": 2,
+  "seed_weight_suburb": 1,
+  "seed_weight_quarter": 3,
+  "seed_weight_neighbourhood": 1
+}
+```
+
+Fail-fast (the catalog's standing bar, ODN-5): missing block → load error
+(defaults to -1, never silent); `district_cap_permille` 1..1000 (0 would
+cap every district at 1 — a silent near-dead board; document 1 as the
+effective floor); weights 0..1000 (0 = the band excluded — a deliberate
+tunable, not a data error; the weighted pick skips non-positive weights by
+construction). All integers (ODN-10), folded into catalog_hash like every
+sibling block (the re-bless cause).
+
+## 3. Tests (the pin list)
+
+1. **Assignment pins (map_test):** nearest-anchor assignment deterministic
+   (tie-break = lower district index); every pool tile assigned to exactly
+   one district; per-district tile lists partition the pool; zero-tile
+   districts hold empty lists; `district_assign` agrees with the load-time
+   lists.
+2. **SEED weighted draw (growth_test, fixture board):** with two districts
+   of unequal weights, the weighted district receives the majority of
+   seeds (statistical over many windows, seed-averaged — deterministic);
+   a capped district stops receiving seeds; a zero-weight band never
+   receives seeds; a district with one tile draws without the tile pick.
+3. **ATTACH cluster-pick weighting:** two eligible estates at DISTINCT
+   weights (city 4 vs suburb 1) — the rich district's estate extends
+   measurably more over deterministic windows (the accepted ratio lands
+   below the raw 4:1 — A's ring saturates first and its picks reject more;
+   the honest 1.5× bar, mutation-verified: the uniform-pick mutation
+   flips the sample to dead-even 27:27 and FAILS the pin); a cluster whose
+   district is at cap is ineligible; the drawn TILE's district is
+   cap-checked (W1).
+4. **Cap contract:** a district at cap blocks BOTH families (seeds go
+   elsewhere; the cluster is not extended). The budget is the live count —
+   the freeing clause is vacuous-by-design (r1 W2): terminal demolish is
+   E2-forbidden, so the count is monotone within a run.
+5. **E31 + pool invariants (unchanged contracts):** every spawn on a pool
+   tile, pairwise min-separation, connectable-within-span, strict-radius
+   attach closure, fresh-area seed floor — the existing board tests must
+   pass UNCHANGED (they pin the streets rule).
+6. **Replay byte-identity:** a growing dublin run replays byte-identically
+   (the existing spine test extended to the board + the new draws).
+7. **Procedural inertness:** procedural growth draws exactly the old rng
+   stream (the full golden suite — 48/48 byte-identical, zero re-bless).
+8. **Catalog fail-fast rows:** missing block, out-of-range cap, out-of-range
+   weights → named load errors (the table convention).
+9. **Mirror fixture:** `test_catalog` carries the REAL defaults (the
+   mirror-fixture rule — a zeroed weight/cap silently changes test
+   semantics).
+
+## 4. Verification
+
+- `tools/ci-local.sh --mac` (all 13 gates; rebuild `bin/harness` from the
+  worktree with the main checkout's raylib-sw shadow before the golden
+  gate).
+- Dual-run determinism: procedural suite byte-identical; `dublin_board.dem`
+  re-blessed with the cause documented; `cmp -l` every `.log.bin`/`.t1` vs
+  HEAD (expect exactly the deliberate deltas).
+- KYLE mock-match gate (rule 2): live captures of the grown board (baywide
+  + templebar zoom) vs the approved mock visuals
+  (`docs/captures/dublin-map-mock/`) — KYLE compares spawn behavior against
+  the approved state, verdict recorded in the PR body.
+- pr_review: 1 (the Perkins loop follows).
+
+## 5. Out of scope (named)
+
+Streets-constrain-pipes (stage-2 job 2), last-mile draw (stage-2 job 3),
+zoom-LOD render bands, dublin.json re-bake, osm_extract changes, procedural
+terrain, any router spawning.
